  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Universal File Attachments",
      "text": "Session-scoped universal file attachments for [DeepSeek Harness (DSH)](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-Harness).\n\nIt replaces path injection with a compact attachment rail: images, videos,\naudio, documents, archives, unknown files, and folders are kept as safe,\nsession-scoped attachments. Browser and agent tooling receive attachment IDs,\nnever a local machine path."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Drag or paste files directly into a DSH conversation. No extra picker UI.\n- Preview images and videos; show type cards for documents, audio, archives,\n  folders, and other files.\n- Chunked uploads with SHA-256 finalization and a 2 GB per-file / 10 GB batch\n  limit.\n- Session, tenant, user, and agent isolation on every host route.\n- Agent tools for listing, reading, extracting, searching, materializing, and\n  explicitly importing attachments into an asset or knowledge service.\n- Safe folder manifests: relative paths only; `.git`, `node_modules`,\n  `.DS_Store`, device files, and unsafe paths are rejected."
    },
    {
      "section": "Platform support",
      "text": "The plugin is implemented with Node.js and standard Chromium browser APIs and\nworks on macOS, Windows 10/11, and Linux when DSH runs on a supported Node.js\nruntime."
    },
    {
      "section": "Platform support",
      "text": "| Capability | Windows Chrome / Edge | macOS Chrome | Firefox |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| File drag and paste | Supported | Supported | Supported |\n| Image / video previews | Supported | Supported | Supported |\n| Folder drag with directory tree | Supported | Supported | Browser fallback only |\n| Chunked file upload | Supported | Supported | Supported |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Platform support",
      "text": "Folder traversal uses the File System Access API when available, then the\nstandard Chromium directory entry API, then the browser file list. Use current\nChrome or Edge for complete folder-tree support on Windows."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "From a local clone:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/13323232dong/dsh-file-attachments.git\ncd dsh-file-attachments\nnpm install\nnpm run build\n\nRestart the DSH web process after installation. The plugin occupies the\n`conversation.input.attachments` slot with a higher-priority universal rail,\nso remove other plugins that independently consume document-level file-drop\nevents."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "The core attachment store works without external services. Optional explicit\nimports to an OPC-compatible asset or knowledge API need server-side settings:\n\n```yaml\n- id: opc-file-attachments\n  config:\n    apiBaseUrl: https://your-opc-api.example\n    identityHmacSecret: !!js process.env.OPC_DSH_IDENTITY_HMAC_SECRET\n\nNever expose `identityHmacSecret` to the browser. The browser sends only its\ncurrent DSH session ID; the host resolves the principal and signs outbound\nrequests."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\nnpm install\nnpm test\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm run build"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
